#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
SYNTAX IRS / BSA Filing Cypher Diagnostician

Decodes the coded fields ("cyphers") carried by IRS- and FinCEN-administered
financial reports, runs diagnostic checks over them, and converts surviving
findings into evasion signals consumable by the SANCTIONS module.

Covered instruments:
    Form 8300   - cash received over $10,000 in a trade or business (IRS)
    FBAR / 114  - report of foreign bank and financial accounts (FinCEN/IRS)
    CTR / 112   - currency transaction report (FinCEN)
    SAR / 111   - suspicious activity report (FinCEN)
    Form 8938   - statement of specified foreign financial assets (FATCA)
    Form 926    - return by a transferor of property to a foreign corporation

IMPORTANT - code tables below are structural models carrying representative
values, not an authoritative transcription. Thresholds, category codes, and
filing deadlines change; validate CYPHER_TABLES and REPORTING_THRESHOLDS
against the current IRS and FinCEN instructions before operational use. The
diagnostician reports where a filing looks inconsistent; it does not determine
that any filing is wrong, and it makes no finding about any person.

All sample filings shipped with --demo are synthetic.

Copyright 2025 - Apache License 2.0
"""

